WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.186
The Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.329
The law that doesn't protect.

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:10.136
Canada's whistleblower protection legislation was enacted in 2007.

00:00:10.136 --> 00:00:15.000
It was supposed to create a safe mechanism for public servants to report wrongdoing.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.113
Instead, the Act protects the institution.

00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:21.124
Reprisal complaints take years to resolve.

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:23.988
Successful protections are near zero.

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:29.499
Whistleblowers who report are more likely to face career destruction than the wrongdoers they expose.

00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:30.931
The Act.

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:44.954
The Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act, enacted in 2007, creates two bodies: the Public Sector Integrity Commissioner, who receives disclosures of wrongdoing, and the Public Servants Disclosure Protection Tribunal, which adjudicates reprisal complaints.

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:48.306
The Act prohibits reprisal against whistleblowers.

00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:52.102
In practice: reprisal complaints take years to resolve.

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:55.090
The Tribunal has rarely ordered remedies.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:00.659
Multiple Integrity Commissioners have been criticized for failing to investigate disclosures adequately.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:02.704
The protection inversion.

00:01:02.704 --> 00:01:06.579
The Act is named the Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act.

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:09.715
It protects the disclosure — meaning the document.

00:01:09.715 --> 00:01:13.613
It does not effectively protect the person who makes the disclosure.

00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:15.965
The whistleblower is exposed.

00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:21.715
The wrongdoer is shielded by cabinet confidence, by the chain of command, by the investigation timeline.

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:27.465
By the time the system responds, the whistleblower's career is over and the wrongdoer has been promoted.

00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:36.659
This is the same institutional architecture documented across every TENET5 investigation: the accountability mechanism protects the institution, not the citizen.
